## Readiness Gate Transfer

1. `G1-EXECUTIVE-INTENT-AUTHORITY` — narrow singleton intent source with no duplicate execution authority.
2. `G2-STRATEGIC-COCKPIT-EXPERIENCE` — concise decision surface and explicit ledger drill-down.
3. `G3-PARITY-RECOVERY-AND-OWNER-ACCEPTANCE` — deterministic portable behavior and owner scenarios.

## Program Shape

Deliver one bounded Work1 candidate. Implement the managed intent contract, revise the executive
projection and command interface, remove the main ledger, update docs and the portable skill, run
focused and full local validation, checkpoint only the corrective work, and stop without deployment
or release.

## Constraints And Non-Goals

- No production publication, remote deployment, hosted write-back, or client synchronization.
- No DisplayTest migration without its directly available source and a separate no-loss review.
- No manual editing of generated `work/100k.md`.
- No autonomous strategy selection from a read-only review.
- No second project-world builder, strategic backlog, database, or lifecycle system.

## Completion Boundary

This map is complete when all three transferred gates pass in one locally verified Work1 candidate
and the candidate is checkpointed with IDEA-0029's outcome chain still open for any later delivery
or field evidence.
